<title>USA: Orange County, Fla., mulls sales tax referendum.</title>
<headline>Orange County, Fla., mulls sales tax referendum.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Fla. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida's Orange County Commission will decide by Aug. 5 whether to seek a November referendum on a one-cent sales tax increase, a county spokeswoman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The proposal would increase the county's sales tax to 7 percent for six years, raising about $1 billion.</p>
<p>County schools would receive 30 percent of the revenues and the rest would be used for highways, parks and stormwater improvements.</p>
<p>Spokeswoman Shelly Poore said bond financing is not anticipated for any of the projects.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
